name spawn_stand
describe The cheapest smoke test: spawn at the default pose, stand still for three seconds, capture the frame the world becomes visible and the last frame. It is the first thing to run after any change, because it fails for the largest number of reasons -- a broken shader, a broken build, a broken tree, an empty frame -- in six seconds instead of six minutes.
backend both

# TAA off for every scenario that compares a capture against a golden. Measured, not assumed:
# with TAA on, vk-vs-vk moves 0.996% of pixels at this pose against a 1.5% gate, and with it off
# 0.341% -- see dev/harness/src/image_compare.hpp for the full four-case table.
option --no-taa

# Prompt 007 goal 344: --no-wind, and it is a CAPTURE-REPRODUCIBILITY requirement rather than a
# preference. Goals 333/335/338 put moving content in every frame -- a ground shimmer, swaying trees
# and grass -- and all of it is driven by an animation clock that is the WALL CLOCK by default. So a
# golden of this pose stopped being reproducible: the "final" capture measured 9.27% of pixels
# changed against a 1.5% gate on a scene where nothing moves but the wind. `--anim-step` makes the
# clock deterministic per FRAME, which is not enough on its own, because `capture end` lands on a
# different frame index between runs (goal 337 records that limit). Killing the wind for the capture
# scenarios is what the project already does for every wind A/B -- goal 332's own 0.0012% number was
# measured that way -- and it leaves the golden measuring everything else: terrain, tree shape,
# grass geometry, shading, LOD.
option --no-wind

pose_ground 48,0 -90 -10 1.7
wait 3

# Prompt 007 goal 344: NO GOLDEN on this one, and the reason is what it is timed on. `first_light`
# fires on the world-ready EVENT, whose frame index moves between runs -- the build is threaded and
# finishes when it finishes. With a static world that did not matter; with goal 338's grass and
# goal 335's trees in the frame it does, and re-taken it still reads 1.652% of pixels changed
# against a 1.5% gate (at a mean distance of 0.502/255, i.e. everywhere-slightly rather than
# somewhere-badly). Prompt 003's rule applies: a capture that is not reproducible does not get a
# golden, it gets a note. `final` below IS golden-compared, because `capture end` lands on a settled
# world.
capture event world-ready first_light no-golden
capture end final

assert frames > 0
assert contrast_percent > 6
assert walk_violations == 0
assert inside_solid == 0
